## PROJECT ARCHITECTURE — MVC Pattern

"I structured the backend following the MVC architecture pattern
with clear separation of concerns across 4 layers:"

```
HTTP Request from Browser/Postman
           ↓
    CONTROLLER LAYER
    (Receives request, sends response)
           ↓
    SERVICE LAYER
    (Business logic — rules of the application)
           ↓
    REPOSITORY LAYER
    (Talks to the database using JPA)
           ↓
    DATABASE (MySQL)
```

### What each package does:

- model/       → Java classes that map to database tables (@Entity)
- repository/  → Interfaces that query the database (extends JpaRepository)
- service/     → Business logic — all rules and calculations
- controller/  → REST API endpoints — receives HTTP requests
- dto/         → Data Transfer Objects — shape of request/response data
- security/    → JWT filter and utility — protects API routes
- config/      → Spring Security configuration

